{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_ae467c060b9e267700ffbd7a926a5535bae9ad191c1f00818d6c9fffa300ee1b", "title": "Ave Maria Gyrenes", "text": "The Ave Maria University Gyrenes are the athletic teams for Ave Maria University in Ave Maria, Florida.", "score": 21.8216}, {"id": "hp_doc_06b43f1db4b004a4aa53cb9a7b391129f2f04fa7f33f94a2be5387e371173a48", "title": "Calendar Girl (Sophie Monk album)", "text": "Calendar Girl is the debut solo studio album by Australian recording artist Sophie Monk, released on 5 May 2003 by Warner Music. It debuted at No. 35 March 2003 on the ARIA Albums Chart top 50. The album was mixed with contemporary pop as well as the religious classics tracks \"Pie Jesu\", \"Ave Maria\" (Interlude) and \"Ave Maria\".", "score": 20.5481}, {"id": "hp_doc_b88cc285c4c292705757669489957059798819f4aceaa1d09f3cc3beec4a82f0", "title": "Ave Maria (Beyoncé song)", "text": "\"Ave Maria\" is a song by American R&B recording artist Beyoncé Knowles from her third studio album \"I Am... Sasha Fierce\" (2008). Amanda Ghost, Ian Dench and Makeba Riddick wrote the song in collaboration with its producers Knowles and production duo Stargate. As stated by Ghost, \"Ave Maria\" was inspired by Knowles' and her own respective marriages. The song is a re-write of Franz Schubert's \"Ave Maria\". It is instrumentally complete with a piano and strings. Throughout the ballad, Knowles sings in a lower register with an operatic soprano. Lyrically, it speaks about being surrounded by friends but still feeling alone.", "score": 20.1416}], "remaining_searches": 2}
